From 94a3e3f42f7695c3e12e4fb746f2a59a1a81a43a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 21:09:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v1.4.6: navigation cleanup - hide superseded +
 duplicate pages

UI/navigation only; no underlying feature change. Both build variants.

Hide "Open NAT" (menuTree.js + Main_ReaperDash.asp):
- Remove the menu_OpenNAT static section; make its retArray hide unconditional
  (was gated on gameMode_support, comment wrongly said "keep").
- Remove the "Open NAT" dashboard-rail tile (pointed at Main_GameServer_Content.asp).
- Port forwarding itself is unchanged / still reachable.

Remove the QoS "Related Pages" block (Reaper_QoS.asp):
- Delete the linkspanel block. It linked the two legacy QoS editors (suppressed
  below) plus the kept Bandwidth Limiter editor (QoS_EZQoS.asp); preserve that one
  as a contextual .modelink inside the Bandwidth Limiter mode card so the mode
  isn't stranded.

Suppress superseded stock pages (menuTree.js + reaper_inject.c):
- Menu: remove the 5 stock Traffic Monitor pages, TrafficAnalyzer_Statistic.asp,
  and the 2 legacy QoS editors (Advanced_QOSUserPrio/UserRules_Content.asp). Keep
  Reaper_Traffic, Reaper_QoS, and Traffic Limiter.
- URL: extend the injected bounce script with a suppression map (SUP{}) that
  redirects any direct/framed hit on those 8 pages to their reaper-native
  replacement (Traffic Monitor/Statistic -> Reaper_Traffic; legacy QoS ->
  Reaper_QoS), in both top and framed contexts (top.location).

Both v1.4.6 images built + verified (noMCP zero-trace clean; 8 suppression
targets baked into httpd; rail/Related-Pages removed; BW link kept).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
